<title>GERMANY: Siemens unit sees stable Q1 sales, orders.</title>
<headline>Siemens unit sees stable Q1 sales, orders.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified manufacturer Siemens AG said on Monday its automation unit (AUT) saw stable sales and orders in the first quarter of the 1996/97 business year.</p>
<p>AUT, which builds material handling systems, had sales of 6.6 billion marks and pretax profit of 509 million marks in 1995/96, which ended September 30. Orders rose seven percent last year to six billion marks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, +49-228 26097150</p>
</text>
